# Integer128 multiplication within range

Multiplies 10^19 by 10^10, then the negated left operand by the same
right operand, to verify the products stay inside the 128-bit range in
both signs, producing 100000000000000000000000000000 and its negation.

>>> source
left: int128 = 10000000000000000000
right: int128 = 10000000000
neg_left: int128 = -10000000000000000000

// Verifies multiplication of two positive operands.
pos_product: int128 = left * right
print(pos_product)

// Verifies multiplication with opposite signs.
mixed_product: int128 = neg_left * right
print(mixed_product)

<<< stdout
100000000000000000000000000000
-100000000000000000000000000000

<<< stderr
